// Rule: [T1059.007][T1036] Teams Helpdesk Intrusion - Node Wscript Localappdata Loader
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.007, T1036
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Defender XDR hunt for the source-observed WScript bootstrap launching portable Node.js from a user-writable directory without a JavaScript file on the child command line.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for node wscript localappdata loader using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: successful exploitation, malicious ownership, downstream impact, campaign attribution or complete compromise without corroborating evidence.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Portable Node.js launched by WScript from LocalAppData
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceProcessEvents
// Evidence: Microsoft Security Research, published 2026-09-02.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "node.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine has @"\AppData\Local\"
    and ProcessCommandLine !contains ".js"
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "wscript.exe"
| where InitiatingProcessCommandLine has_all (@"\AppData\Local\", "node.exe", ".js")
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, ActionType,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName,
          SHA1, ProcessId, ProcessCreationTime,
          AccountDomain, AccountName, AccountSid, AccountUpn,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessId,
          InitiatingProcessCreationTime, InitiatingProcessSHA1,
          InitiatingProcessAccountDomain, InitiatingProcessAccountName,
          InitiatingProcessAccountSid, InitiatingProcessAccountUpn,
          InitiatingProcessIntegrityLevel, InitiatingProcessTokenElevation,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
